Let each side of the square be distance \(s\). Total distance is \(4s\). Time taken is sum of times for each side: \(\frac{s}{200}+\frac{s}{400}+\frac{s}{600}+\frac{s}{800}\). Average speed is total distance divided by total time:  
\[
\frac{4s}{s(\frac{1}{200}+\frac{1}{400}+\frac{1}{600}+\frac{1}{800})}
= \frac{4}{\frac{1}{200}+\frac{1}{400}+\frac{1}{600}+\frac{1}{800}}
\]
The sum of reciprocals is \(\frac{25}{2400}=\frac{1}{96}\), so average speed is \(4 \div \frac{1}{96}=384\) km/hr.
